implementationPlan.description:
scripts/local-runner/guest-supervisor.py, LAUNCH['codex'] (~:793-794): the config text gains `env_vars = ["MOE_ROLE"]\n` right after the command line. The result is exactly LA_CONFIG.codex with the guest SHIM path.

Add a one-line comment beside LAUNCH explaining why: codex 0.166 starts a stdio MCP server with only HOME, PATH and LC_CTYPE, and env_vars forwards exactly MOE_ROLE, the one variable guest-mcp-shim.py main() reads, never the credential.

Leave everything else as it is:
- claude's .moe-mcp.json, argv, PROMPTS and SHIM;
- the (executable, credential names) shape of JOBS, so B17 and AGENT_JOBS still hold;
- prepare_launch's O_EXCL|O_NOFOLLOW creation;
- start_job's env (it already sets MOE_ROLE from the validated frame role, ~:898);
- every other supervisor mode.

Error handling: unchanged. A config write failure still returns 71 with no job, as before.

VERIFY ONCE, fresh, on WSL:

env -i HOME="$HOME" PATH="$HOME/.nvm/versions/node/v24.21.0/bin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin" MOE_PINNED_CODEX=/tmp/r10d4-evidence/codex-x86_64-unknown-linux-musl node --test scripts/tests/local-runner-bridge.test.mjs scripts/tests/local-runner-agents.test.mjs

It must exit 0, and the TAP output must show LA5 passed, not skipped. Its command, exit code and output tail are complete_task's verification evidence.

If /tmp/r10d4-evidence is gone, set the pinned codex up outside the repository:
- download agent-binaries.json's codex x64 URL into a fresh scratch dir;
- check the archive's sha256;
- extract the member, check memberSha256, and point MOE_PINNED_CODEX at it.

Then run these mutants, on scratch copies of the two files only, and restore and cmp afterwards. Each must turn the named rows red:
(i) drop the env_vars line: LA2, LA3 and LA5;
(ii) `env_vars = ["MOE_ROLE", "CODEX_API_KEY"]`: LA2's credential guard and LA5;
(iii) a literal `env = { MOE_ROLE = "worker" }` instead of env_vars: LA2, and LA5 for qa.

A read-only `git status --short` must show only the two files changed by this task. Never revert, stash, `git add -A` or commit peer or pre-existing paths. Error handling: if a test fails in a file this task did not touch, report it with the output; do not edit it.
